{"summary":"Accepted the amendments that identify live compatibility or state-consistency defects in legacy algae parameter handling, shrimp condition/state updates, and snapshot parsing. Rejected the amendments that are already implemented or rely on stale assumptions about the current substrate default/test behavior.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-bbde1d06","decision":"accept","rationale":"`ProcessParams` still accepts `algae_half_saturation_*_mg_total` via serde alias in `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs`, while `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs` has no migration that renames or rescales those algae fields. A legacy save value like `5.0` therefore deserializes as `5.0 mg/L` instead of the intended `0.25 mg/L`, so the compatibility bug is real."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-b5ce6a89","decision":"reject","rationale":"This plant-save migration gap is already handled. `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs` has `migrate_v7_to_v8()` that removes `plant_half_saturation_*_mg_total`, writes the canonical water/substrate fields with the correct conversions, and `crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs` covers non-default legacy values. The claimed silent reset is not present in the current code."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-bc482e98","decision":"reject","rationale":"The premise is incorrect for the current code. `SubstrateLayerState::default()` in `crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs` sets `colonizable_area_factor` to `0.0`, and `resolved_colonizable_area_factor()` falls back to `kind.default_colonizable_area_factor()`. A `CoarsePorous` layer built with `..Default::default()` still resolves to `0.9`, so this test is not broken for the stated reason."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-f57688d0","decision":"accept","rationale":"Legacy algae preset keys are still accepted by serde aliases on `ProcessParamsPreset`, but `normalize_legacy_process_params_preset()` only rewrites legacy plant keys. That means old algae preset values are loaded without the required `/20` conversion, preserving the same 20x error on the preset path. The defect is real, even if the robust fix should be applied on the preset-parse path rather than only in provenance normalization."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-4901e64f","decision":"accept","rationale":"`shrimp_feeding()` scales demand by `grazing_access_factor` before computing consumed food, but `update_condition()` recomputes `target_food_g` without that factor. With the default substrate grazing surface, shrimp that eat their full accessible ration are still treated as underfed, so condition and downstream reproduction/maturation are systematically penalized. The demand basis should match feeding."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-17d200a6","decision":"accept","rationale":"`PlayerAction::AddShrimp` in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` increments `adult.count` directly and never goes through `StageCohort::receive_entrants()`. If the adult cohort was empty, stale cohort state such as `condition_index` survives into newly purchased shrimp instead of being reseeded; even when non-empty, newcomer state is never merged. That is a real stage-state consistency bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-dce4c34e","decision":"accept","rationale":"`TankSnapshotRepr` requires `total_shrimp_count` and `sub_adult_count`, `normalize_snapshot_object()` only handles chemistry aliases, and the TUI deserializes snapshots directly through this path. A snapshot from an older server that lacks the new shrimp-stage fields will fail deserialization instead of defaulting/reconstructing them, so backward compatibility is incomplete."}]}